      "body": "Off Leash update 11/12/2026\n\nIRAN\n•Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps (IRGC) showed off an underground “missile city” in a new video on state TV.\n•Experts who scrutinized the footage spotted signs that the IRGC is developing technologies that could make its missiles more maneuverable and harder to detect and intercept.\n•The video may have been a retort to Pres. Trump’s claim – made hours before the video was released – that “Iran’s head has been cut off” and its military capabilities were “virtually finished.”\n\nSPAIN\n•Spain’s largest trade union group staged its first general strike in 14 years yesterday. Workers are angry about the same thing that Spain’s students and pensioners alike have been demonstrating against: housing affordability. \n•Those old enough to vote will have another chance to be heard in a general election on Nov. 29. That poll is widely seen as a referendum on socialist prime minister Pedro Sánchez’s proposal to solve the problem with rent controls. The opposition says will worsen the crisis by constricting supply.\n•Voters seem to agree. Sánchez’s Spanish Socialist Workers’ Party (PSOE) is trailing the right-leaning People’s Party in polls, with the far-right Vox party gaining ground on the PSOE, too.\n\nHYBRID WAR\n•Hundreds of schools in Ireland, Italy, Northern Ireland, and Scotland were evacuated yesterday after receiving email bomb threats that turned out to be fake. \n•European officials say the hoaxes were designed to cause confusion and sow chaos. Some suspect a link to other grey zone disruptions like recent cyberattacks on supermarket refrigerators and blood banks. It’s not certain who’s behind them, but Russia still looks like the likeliest culprit.",
